# Raw captures hold live OTPs, bearer tokens, session cookies and the phone
# number that logged in. They never belong in the repo, on a share, or in any
# chat. Keep them here, read them locally, delete them when the contract is
# written. Only a REDACTED analysis (produced by analyze_flows.py) is safe to
# keep, and even that gets eyeballed first.
captures/
*.flows
*.har
*.pem
*.key
wireguard*.conf
# The redacted report is opt-in to commit; ignore by default so it is a choice.
contract-*.md
